  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nShowers linger in the vicinity of a stalled front to the north this \nmorning, while a shortwave brings additional precipitation across \nthe southern half of the forecast area. Scattered showers and \na few thunderstorms will remain possible through the afternoon, \nthen precipitation should taper off for tonight as the front \nslides away from the area and an upper ridge starts building in \nfrom the west.\n\nContinued precipitation will maintain at least a low risk of\nexcessive rainfall across portions of the area today, \nparticularly in areas impacted by heavier rainfall over the \npast day.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nHeat will intensify as an upper level ridge builds east and\nbecomes centered over the region during the work week. Daily\nhigh temperatures are expected to reach 90s in the lowlands,\nwhile humidity makes it feel even hotter. Expect heat indices to\nreach triple digits in the afternoons, particularly from Tuesday\nonward. Already elevated heat risk is likely to be compounded \nby the multiple day stretch of hot weather.",
